{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773093568,"nonce":"AYa2Xdpku6euW97uMMtE+XSQKGs=","title":"Console RichView: stream events not delivered to TerminalPane (payload wrapper mismatch)","message":"Root cause: f9775df changed consoleStreamHandler in app.tsx to spread `{...payload}` into the CustomEvent detail instead of `{...payload.data}`.\n\nThe SSE broadcast sends: { type: \"console:stream_event\", data: { console_session_id, event }, timestamp }\nThe SSE client delivers: payload = { type, data: { console_session_id, event }, timestamp }\n\nTerminalPane reads: detail.console_session_id and detail.event\nAfter the fix: detail = { type, data: { ... }, timestamp } → detail.console_session_id is undefined → all events filtered out\n\nFix: restore payload.data extraction in consoleStreamHandler:\n```\nconst consoleStreamHandler = (payload: SSEPayload) =\u003e {\n  const data = typeof payload.data === \"object\" \u0026\u0026 payload.data \\!== null ? payload.data : payload;\n  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\"console:stream_event\", { detail: data }));\n};\n```\n\nLabels: error","files":null}]}